# Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile actually COPYs: requirements
# and the jarvis package.
#
# Two reasons, and the second one is the load-bearing one.
#
# 1. ./config holds secrets.yaml and the recorder database. There is no reason
#    to hand those to the build daemon.
# 2. Every bind mount in docker-compose.yml is a *relative* path, so its host
#    side lives inside this build context and fills up as the stack runs:
#    ./photon is a geocoding index (tens of GB for the planet extract),
#    ./wyoming/whisper and ./wyoming/piper are downloaded models, ./ollama is
#    model weights. Without the entries below, `docker compose build` after the
#    first run uploads all of that to the daemon before it reads the Dockerfile.
#    Add a matching line here whenever you add a relative bind mount.
config/
photon/
wyoming/
# The embedding and reranker weights TEI downloads (M33), same reasoning
# as wyoming/: fetched once, hundreds of megabytes, never in an image.
models/
# The gateway's config and its guard are bind-mounted into the LiteLLM
# container, not built into any image here.
gateway/
ollama/
searxng/
mosquitto/
tests/
docs/
*.md

.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Runtime state, if anyone ever runs Jarvis from the repo root.
.storage/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.log
.env
